// Probably Weather — bespoke witty lines, keyed to the photograph.
//
// The witty line has always been chosen by CONDITION: a pool of storm lines, a
// pool of wind lines, one picked at random. That is why the same line could land
// on a picture it had nothing to do with, and why review/PAIRING-TASTE.md's
// finding 0 exists — of 214 lines proposed three or more times, 174 got
// different verdicts on different images. Al judges the PAIR.
//
// These lines are written FOR one photograph and only ever appear on it. Al
// ruled every one of them (rounds 1 and 2, 2026-08-18: 210 of 235 kept, 89%,
// against 60% for the condition bank). Authoring file:
// review/set-001-lines-bespoke-final.json, keyed by image hash — one hash can
// occupy two rotation slots and the lines belong to the picture, not the slot.
//
// ENGLISH ONLY, and that is a ruling rather than a gap. Al writes the Afrikaans
// himself, and zu/xh/st go to the native-review backlog — a machine-translated
// joke is not a joke. Every other language keeps the condition bank, which is
// why the lookup is gated on lang below rather than falling back per string.
//
// EXPANDED to slot paths by scripts/build-hero-lines.mjs, because the path is
// what the picker hands the browser. Both key shapes ship for the same reason
// hero-crop.js ships both: the source tree serves slot paths and production
// serves content-addressed names.

